# ALLOW-LIST build context (issue #255). A Docker build sends the WORKING TREE, so a
# deny-list silently shipped every local folder nobody remembered to list (test-instance
# keyfiles, databases, API keys and logins under .test-instances/, sample docs, logs).
# Now NOTHING is sent to the builder unless a `!` line below names it, so a new local
# folder can never reach the image by default.
#
# The list is exactly what the image needs to build and run:
#   * the application package, its migrations and runtime assets (fonts for images);
#   * the entrypoint, pyproject.toml (release fallback version) and the dependency locks;
#   * scripts/saml_smoke.py (the SAML build smoke) and scripts/convert_db_encryption.py
#     (imported by `loc-tms db encrypt|decrypt`);
#   * the license files (LICENSE, NOTICE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
# Anything else (tests, docs, deploy, tools, data, .env, .claude, ...) stays
# out. tests/verify_docker_image.py fails when a runtime reference is not allow-listed
# here or when a secret-bearing or gitignored path could slip back in.

*

!app/
!alembic/
!alembic.ini
!assets/
!docker-entrypoint.sh
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.lock
!requirements-postgres.lock
!requirements-saml.lock
!scripts/locks/requirements-saml-lxml.lock
!scripts/locks/requirements-build.lock
!requirements-ldap.lock
!requirements-sqlcipher.lock
!scripts/saml_smoke.py
!scripts/convert_db_encryption.py
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!README.md

# Re-excluded inside the allowed folders: bytecode, editor cruft, and anything
# secret-shaped that a local run could leave behind.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/.enc_key
**/.session_secret
app/resources/tbx/*.rng
app/resources/tbx/*.sch
app/resources/tbx/*.tbx
